/T (However, Li-Fi is not poised to replace Wi-Fi entirely but rather to complement it  in hybrid networks. Its adoption hinges on standardization, cost reduction, and  device compatibility. The IEEE 802.11bb standard, released in 2023, has formalized  Li-Fi protocols, paving the way for broader integration. Research is also advancing  in using infrared or ultraviolet for non-visible light communication, mitigating  issues like ambient light interference.)
