/E (16-Key Matrix Layout: Arranged in 4 rows and 4 columns, providing 16 buttons labeled with numbers \(0-9\), letters \(A-D\), and symbols \(*, #\) for versatile input options like numeric codes or menu navigation. Compact Design: Typically measures around 70 x 77 mm, lightweight \(about 20-30 grams\), and slim, making it easy to integrate into space-constrained projects. Matrix Configuration: Uses 8 pins \(4 rows, 4 columns\) for interfacing, reducing the number of microcontroller pins needed compared to individual button setups, optimizing I/O usage. Low Power Consumption: Operates at 3.3V to 5V, drawing minimal current \(a few mA per key press\), suitable for battery-powered applications.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [6]
